[{"updatedAt":"2026-05-04T16:45:08.698Z","createdAt":"2026-02-12T17:56:52.881Z","id":"5bE1T9UI3OnTP63Y","name":"IArvis_main","description":null,"active":true,"isArchived":false,"nodes":[{"parameters":{"httpMethod":"POST","path":"chat","responseMode":"responseNode","options":{}},"type":"n8n-nodes-base.webhook","typeVersion":2.1,"position":[-384,0],"id":"345864e3-1309-4ce1-9b2e-e33763caaf5c","name":"Webhook","webhookId":"59df9e83-fb60-4f31-ace0-4b987d84703e"},{"parameters":{"options":{}},"type":"n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook","typeVersion":1.5,"position":[1712,16],"id":"abaf2a61-8480-46a7-acfe-e2bb8f7089e0","name":"Respond to Webhook"},{"parameters":{"sessionIdType":"customKey","sessionKey":"={{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.chat_id }}"},"type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.memoryPostgresChat","typeVersion":1.3,"position":[1344,240],"id":"b6fd4578-55dd-499a-97bc-2c9bcf0ccd31","name":"Postgres Chat Memory","credentials":{"postgres":{"id":"V7NyxTALs80oCdIt","name":"Postgres account"}}},{"parameters":{"promptType":"define","text":"={{ $json.toJsonString() }}","options":{"systemMessage":"=Your name is {{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.settings.Assistant_name }}. You are a personal AI assistant that helps the user remember important facts about their life.\n\nCRITICAL — ZERO HALLUCINATION POLICY ON USER DATA:\nYou will receive a JSON input with these fields:\n  - \"user_message\": the user's question or statement.\n  - \"actions_executed\": ARRAY of strings listing the actions that DID run during this turn. Possible items: \"SEARCH\", \"STORE\", \"TOOL\". The array is the COMPLETE record — if \"STORE\" is NOT in the array, NO storage happened.\n  - \"retrieved_data_RAG\": data from the vector database, OR the literal string \"NONE\" if nothing was retrieved or if SEARCH did not run.\n  - \"retrieved_data_graph\": data from the graph database, OR the literal string \"NONE\" if nothing was retrieved or if SEARCH did not run.\n\nZERO HALLUCINATION RULES:\n\n(A) About the user's data: If retrieved_data_RAG and retrieved_data_graph are both \"NONE\" (or contain nothing relevant to the user's question), tell the user you don't have that information stored. NEVER invent, guess, infer, or assume any user-specific fact. retrieved_data may contain items that are NOT directly relevant (semantic matches that aren't true answers) — if none of the items actually answer the question, say you don't have that specific info.\n\n(B) About actions: read the `actions_executed` array LITERALLY.\n  - If the array is empty `[]` → NO action ran. DO NOT add any \"(Stored.)\" or \"(Search performed.)\" tag at the end. Just answer the user's message naturally.\n  - If the array contains \"SEARCH\" → SEARCH ran. End with something like \"(Search performed.)\".\n  - If the array contains \"STORE\" → STORE ran. End with something like \"(Stored.)\".\n  - If the array contains \"TOOL\" → TOOL ran. End with something like \"(Tool executed.)\".\n  - Multiple items → combine: \"(Search and store performed.)\".\nNEVER claim an action ran if it's not in the array. NEVER omit confirming an action that IS in the array.\n\nYou are the final node of a multi-agent system.\n\nTone: {{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.settings.Assistant_tone }}.\n\nReasoning steps:\n1. Read the input JSON.\n2. If the user's message asks about their personal life AND both retrieved_data fields are \"NONE\"/empty:\n     → Reply: \"I don't have that information stored yet.\" (adapted to tone) and confirm any STORE/TOOL action that did run.\n3. If retrieved_data fields contain relevant info: build the answer using ONLY that info as the source of truth for user-specific facts.\n4. If the message is general knowledge (no DB lookup needed): answer with your own knowledge.\n5. At the end, briefly confirm which actions were performed (only the ones whose flag is true).\n\nRules:\n- NEVER fabricate user-specific data. If you don't have it from retrieved_data, you don't have it.\n- Be concise. No suggestions or unsolicited advice.\n- Admit when you don't know something.\n- Do not describe your purpose or capabilities.\n- Do not ask many questions.\n\nExamples:\n\nInput: {\"user_message\":\"Hello!\",\"actions_executed\":[],\"retrieved_data_RAG\":\"NONE\",\"retrieved_data_graph\":\"NONE\"}\nOutput: Hi there! How can I help?\n\nInput: {\"user_message\":\"I want to go to the movies tomorrow.\",\"actions_executed\":[],\"retrieved_data_RAG\":\"NONE\",\"retrieved_data_graph\":\"NONE\"}\nOutput: Sounds great. Enjoy the movies.\n\nInput: {\"user_message\":\"Tell me the difference between college and university.\",\"actions_executed\":[],\"retrieved_data_RAG\":\"NONE\",\"retrieved_data_graph\":\"NONE\"}\nOutput: College often refers to a smaller institution focused on undergraduate education, while university is broader and typically includes both undergraduate and graduate programs.\n\nInput: {\"user_message\":\"Do I like sushi?\",\"actions_executed\":[\"SEARCH\"],\"retrieved_data_RAG\":\"NONE\",\"retrieved_data_graph\":\"NONE\"}\nOutput: I don't have that information stored yet. (Search performed.)\n\nInput: {\"user_message\":\"Do I like coffee?\",\"actions_executed\":[\"SEARCH\"],\"retrieved_data_RAG\":\"- The user likes milk coffee.\",\"retrieved_data_graph\":\"NONE\"}\nOutput: Yes, you like milk coffee. (Search performed.)\n\nInput: {\"user_message\":\"Do I like elephants?\",\"actions_executed\":[\"SEARCH\"],\"retrieved_data_RAG\":\"- The user likes cheese.\\n- The user likes milk coffee.\",\"retrieved_data_graph\":\"NONE\"}\nOutput: I don't have any information about elephants in your stored memory. (Search performed.)\n\nInput: {\"user_message\":\"I love bacon\",\"actions_executed\":[\"STORE\"],\"retrieved_data_RAG\":\"NONE\",\"retrieved_data_graph\":\"NONE\"}\nOutput: Got it — I'll remember you love bacon. (Stored.)\n\nInput: {\"user_message\":\"Can you remember how much I like chocolate?\",\"actions_executed\":[\"SEARCH\",\"STORE\"],\"retrieved_data_RAG\":\"NONE\",\"retrieved_data_graph\":\"NONE\"}\nOutput: I don't have any chocolate-related preferences stored yet, but I've noted your preference now. (Search and store performed.)"}},"type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent","typeVersion":3.1,"position":[1248,16],"id":"48cc8798-bace-47eb-acd2-ac428ea0518a","name":"AGENT"},{"parameters":{"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"c55470d9-f20d-4bc2-8114-f1f83a252c38","name":"user_message","value":"={{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.message }}","type":"string"},{"id":"d12aa494-359e-450f-ac97-d3dc54efc699","name":"actions_executed","value":"={{ $('ROUTER').item.json.actions.toJsonString() }}","type":"array"},{"id":"4fcfae78-b782-434b-b849-502d64b1d9d1","name":"retrieved_data_RAG","value":"={{ $if($('load data').isExecuted, $('load data').first().json.rag_results , 'NONE')}}","type":"string"},{"id":"771bd763-8a93-4e33-a434-81ed711d77a9","name":"retrieved_data_graph","value":"={{ $if($('load data').isExecuted, $('load data').first().json.graph_results , 'NONE')}}","type":"string"}]},"options":{}},"type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","typeVersion":3.4,"position":[1072,16],"id":"21a448f1-f095-42c9-b5d4-8ea5dbea52ed","name":"Data to agent","executeOnce":true},{"parameters":{"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"cd0f4c4f-06a1-4936-b7cf-16593dada7f0","name":"response","value":"={{ $json.output }}","type":"string"},{"id":"33850a43-c9a2-4809-8081-933404e148fa","name":"chat_id","value":"={{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.chat_id }}","type":"string"}]},"options":{}},"type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","typeVersion":3.4,"position":[1536,16],"id":"f1443af9-ea2c-4b9c-8b93-65203504cdd2","name":"Data to backend response"},{"parameters":{"rules":{"values":[{"conditions":{"options":{"caseSensitive":true,"leftValue":"","typeValidation":"strict","version":3},"conditions":[{"leftValue":"={{ $json.body.search }}","rightValue":false,"operator":{"type":"boolean","operation":"true","singleValue":true},"id":"5295f4ca-d63c-4f21-b058-d3f91d0fbf3c"}],"combinator":"and"},"renameOutput":true,"outputKey":